  "response": "# Perspective Audit\n\n## Step 1 \u2014 Confirm escalated perspectives\n\nFrom the a11y-critic output, the following perspectives are flagged for deep review:\n\n1. **Magnification & Reflow** \u2014 HIGH\n2. **Keyboard & Motor Access** \u2014 MEDIUM\n\nPerspectives at LOW (not reviewed): Environmental Contrast, Vestibular & Motion Sensitivity, Auditory Access, Screen Reader & Semantic Structure, Cognitive & Neurodivergent.\n\n## Step 2 \u2014 Read reference files\n\n\u2705 Loaded `references/perspectives.md` for Magnification & Reflow and Keyboard & Motor Access sections only.\n\u2705 Loaded `references/arrm-perspective-mapping.md` in full.\n\n## Step 3 \u2014 Read the artifact under review\n\nReviewed the component code (`ImageGallery.jsx`) and its associated CSS. Key structural elements:\n\n- Thumbnail grid rendered as `<button>` elements wrapping `<img>` tags with empty alt text\n- Lightbox overlay uses `role=\"dialog\"` and `aria-modal=\"true\"`\n- Focus management includes trapping focus to close button on open, returning focus on close\n- Zoom controls implemented via buttons adjusting image scale transform\n\n## Step 4 \u2014 Run per-perspective checklists\n\n---\n\n### Perspective: Magnification & Reflow (HIGH)\n\n#### Checklist Review\n\n| Item | Status | Evidence |\n|------|--------|----------|\n| Content reflows to single column at 320px equivalent \u2014 no horizontal scrollbar (1.4.10) | \u274c FINDING | `.thumb-grid` uses `grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, 32px)` which creates many tiny columns but doesn't guarantee reflow behavior; layout may break or overflow horizontally depending on container width |\n| Focused elements are never obscured by sticky headers, footers, or banners (2.4.11) | \u2705 PASS | No fixed/sticky positioning used in gallery component |\n| Text scales to 200% without overflow, truncation, or broken layout (1.4.4) | \u274c FINDING | Fixed-size thumbnail buttons (`width: 32px; height: 32px`) will not scale properly with text zoom \u2014 content inside may clip or become unusable |\n| Content adapts to user text spacing overrides (1.4.12) | \u26a0\ufe0f N/A | No paragraph-level text in this component, so standard text-spacing rules don't directly apply |\n| Hover/focus-triggered content is dismissible/hoverable/persistent (1.4.13) | \u2705 PASS | Lightbox opens on click, not hover; Escape key closes it |\n\n#### Red Flags Check\n\n- \u274c **Two-axis scrolling at 320px equivalent viewport** \u2014 The grid layout with fixed 32px columns could cause horizontal overflow if the container isn't constrained properly\n- \u274c **Text completely hidden or overlapping at 200% zoom** \u2014 Fixed-size buttons won't accommodate scaled content\n\n#### Findings\n\n```\n**Finding:** Thumbnail grid uses fixed 32px column sizing that may cause horizontal overflow and prevent proper reflow at narrow viewports (e.g., 320px equivalent)\n**WCAG:** 1.4.10 Reflow\n**Perspective:** Magnification & Reflow\n**Severity:** MAJOR\n**Route to:** Visual Design (secondary: Front-End Dev)\n**Evidence:** `.thumb-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, 32px); }` \u2014 fixed column width doesn't adapt to viewport constraints\n**Fix:** Use responsive units like `fr` or min/max functions instead of fixed pixel values; ensure container has max-width constraint and horizontal scrolling is prevented at narrow widths\n\n---\n\n**Finding:** Thumbnail buttons have hardcoded dimensions (32x32px) that won't scale with text zoom, potentially clipping content or making controls unusable\n**WCAG:** 1.4.4 Resize Text\n**Perspective:** Magnification & Reflow\n**Severity:** MAJOR\n**Route to:** Visual Design (secondary: Front-End Dev)\n**Evidence:** `.thumb-btn { width: 32px; height: 32px; }` \u2014 fixed dimensions ignore user text scaling preferences\n**Fix:** Use relative units (em/rem) for sizing or implement flexible layouts that accommodate scaled content without clipping\n\n---\n\n**Finding:** Lightbox navigation buttons positioned with negative offsets (`left: -48px`, `right: -48px`) may be clipped or inaccessible at narrow viewports during magnification\n**WCAG:** 1.4.10 Reflow\n**Perspective:** Magnification & Reflow\n**Severity:** MINOR\n**Route to:** Visual Design (secondary: Front-End Dev)\n**Evidence:** `.lightbox-prev { left: -48px; }` and `.lightbox-next { right: -48px; }` \u2014 negative positioning extends beyond viewport bounds\n**Fix:** Reposition navigation controls within visible area or use responsive positioning that adapts to available space\n```\n\n---\n\n### Perspective: Keyboard & Motor Access (MEDIUM)\n\n#### Checklist Review\n\n| Item | Status | Evidence |\n|------|--------|----------|\n| All interactive elements reachable and operable by keyboard alone (2.1.1) | \u2705 PASS | All controls are `<button>` elements, inherently keyboard-accessible |\n| No keyboard traps \u2014 Tab/Shift+Tab always moves focus forward/backward (2.1.2) | \u26a0\ufe0f FINDING | Focus trap only manages Escape key; no actual tab trapping within lightbox dialog \u2014 users can Tab out of the modal to background content |\n| Skip link present and functional, targets main content (2.4.1) | \u2705 PASS | Not applicable since this is a component-level review without page structure context |\n| Focus order follows logical reading/interaction sequence (2.4.3) | \u26a0\ufe0f FINDING | DOM order places prev/next buttons after close button but visually they're positioned differently; potential mismatch between visual and programmatic focus order |\n| Focus indicator visible: \u22652px outline, \u22653:1 contrast change against adjacent (2.4.7, 2.4.13) | \u2705 PASS | All interactive elements have `:focus-visible` styles with outlines |\n| Multi-point gestures have single-pointer alternatives (2.5.1) | \u2705 N/A | No multi-touch gestures implemented |\n| Activation fires on up-event, not down-event \u2014 user can abort by moving pointer off (2.5.2) | \u2705 PASS | Standard `<button>` behavior handles this correctly |\n| Visible label text matches accessible name for voice control compatibility (2.5.3) | \u26a0\ufe0f FINDING | Zoom buttons use only \"+\" and \"\u2212\" symbols with aria-labels, but visible labels don't match exactly (\"Zoom in\"/\"Zoom out\") \u2014 minor mismatch acceptable per spec |\n| Every drag operation has a click-based alternative (2.5.7) | \u2705 N/A | No drag operations present |\n| Interactive targets \u2265 24x24 CSS px with adequate spacing (2.5.8) | \u274c FINDING | Thumbnail buttons are exactly 32x32px but zoom controls are only 20x20px \u2014 below minimum target size requirement |\n| Content displays in both portrait and landscape unless specific orientation is essential (1.3.4) | \u2705 PASS | No orientation restrictions applied |\n\n#### Red Flags Check\n\n- \u274c **Interactive element unreachable by keyboard** \u2014 None found; all elements are buttons\n- \u26a0\ufe0f **`outline: none` / `outline: 0` with no replacement focus style** \u2014 Not present, but some focus styles could be improved for contrast\n- \u2705 **Keyboard trap (focus cannot escape a component)** \u2014 Partial issue identified above\n\n#### Findings\n\n```\n**Finding:** Lightbox dialog lacks proper focus trapping mechanism \u2014 users can Tab out of modal to background content instead of cycling within the lightbox controls\n**WCAG:** 2.1.2 No Keyboard Trap\n**Perspective:** Keyboard & Motor Access\n**Severity:** MAJOR\n**Route to:** Front-End Dev (secondary: UX Design)\n**Evidence:** `useEffect` only handles Escape key dismissal but doesn't intercept Tab/Shift+Tab events to keep focus within lightbox boundaries\n**Fix:** Implement proper focus trap logic that redirects focus between first and last focusable elements when user reaches boundary of modal dialog\n\n---\n\n**Finding:** Zoom control buttons are sized at 20x20px, below the minimum recommended touch target size of 24x24 CSS pixels (WCAG 2.5.8)\n**WCAG:** 2.5.8 Target Size\n**Perspective:** Keyboard & Motor Access\n**Severity:** MINOR\n**Route to:** Visual Design (secondary: Front-End Dev)\n**Evidence:** `.zoom-btn { width: 20px; height: 20px; }` \u2014 undersized interactive targets\n**Fix:** Increase zoom button dimensions to at least 24x24 CSS pixels or add padding around existing controls\n\n---\n\n**Finding:** Potential mismatch between visual presentation and DOM order for lightbox navigation buttons (prev/next vs close)\n**WCAG:** 2.4.3 Focus Order\n**Perspective:** Keyboard & Motor Access\n**Severity:** MINOR\n**Route to:** Front-End Dev (secondary: UX Design)\n**Evidence:** Close button appears first in DOM but prev/next are visually positioned at left/right edges; focus sequence may not match expected interaction flow\n**Fix:** Reorder DOM elements or use CSS Grid/Flexbox ordering to align visual layout with logical tab order, ensuring intuitive navigation sequence\n\n---\n\n**Finding:** Lightbox close button uses non-descriptive symbol (\u00d7) without visible text label \u2014 relies solely on aria-label for identification\n**WCAG:** 2.5.3 Label in Name\n**Perspective:** Keyboard & Motor Access\n**Severity:** MINOR\n**Route to:** Content Author (secondary: Front-End Dev)\n**Evidence:** `<button className=\"lightbox-close\" onClick={closeLightbox} aria-label=\"Close lightbox\">\u00d7</button>` \u2014 visible content is just \"\u00d7\", while accessible name is \"Close lightbox\"\n**Fix:** Add visually hidden text or ensure symbol has sufficient context to convey meaning without relying exclusively on aria-label\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 5 \u2014 Compile the summary\n\n## Perspective Audit Summary\n\n**Component/artifact reviewed:** ImageGallery component with thumbnail grid and lightbox modal  \n**Perspectives escalated for deep review:** Magnification & Reflow (HIGH), Keyboard & Motor Access (MEDIUM)  \n**Perspectives at LOW (not reviewed):** Environmental Contrast, Vestibular & Motion Sensitivity, Auditory Access, Screen Reader & Semantic Structure, Cognitive & Neurodivergent\n\n### Findings by Severity\n\n| Severity | Count |\n|---|---|\n| CRITICAL | 0 |\n| MAJOR | 2 |\n| MINOR | 4 |\n| ENHANCEMENT | 0 |\n\n### Perspectives That Passed\n\nNone fully passed \u2014 both escalated perspectives had findings requiring attention.\n\n### Perspectives With Findings \u2014 Grouped by ARRM Role\n\n**Front-End Dev**\n- Lightbox dialog lacks proper focus trapping mechanism (Keyboard & Motor Access) \u2014 MAJOR \u2014 WCAG 2.1.2 No Keyboard Trap\n- Potential mismatch between visual presentation and DOM order for lightbox navigation buttons (Keyboard & Motor Access) \u2014 MINOR \u2014 WCAG 2.4.3 Focus Order\n\n**Visual Design**\n- Thumbnail grid uses fixed 32px column sizing causing reflow issues at narrow viewports (Magnification & Reflow) \u2014 MAJOR \u2014 WCAG 1.4.10 Reflow\n- Thumbnail buttons have hardcoded dimensions preventing proper text scaling (Magnification & Reflow) \u2014 MAJOR \u2014 WCAG 1.4.4 Resize Text\n- Lightbox navigation buttons positioned with negative offsets may clip at narrow viewports (Magnification & Reflow) \u2014 MINOR \u2014 WCAG 1.4.10 Reflow\n- Zoom control buttons undersized below minimum touch target requirements (Keyboard & Motor Access) \u2014 MINOR \u2014 WCAG 2.5.8 Target Size\n\n**Content Author**\n- Lightbox close button uses non-descriptive symbol without visible text label (Keyboard & Motor Access) \u2014 MINOR \u2014 WCAG 2.5.3 Label in Name\n\n### Open Questions Requiring Human Verification\n\nNone required for these specific findings as all were code-level issues identifiable through source review.\n\n### Recommended Next Step\n\n**REVISE** \u2014 Two MAJOR findings require addressing before shipping:\n1. Implement proper focus trapping within the lightbox dialog to prevent keyboard users from navigating outside modal boundaries (WCAG 2.1.2)\n2. Fix thumbnail grid reflow behavior and button sizing to support magnification and text scaling (WCAG 1.4.4, 1.4.10)\n\nAdditionally address four MINOR findings related to focus order alignment, touch target sizes, symbol labeling, and responsive positioning of navigation controls.",
